# Researcher

An **auto-researcher** has a fixed shape: **plan → search → verify → synthesize**,
looped. The discipline is the point — a loop that skips `verify` is a confident
hallucinator. Its output is a typed `Dossier`, every finding welded to a source.

defmodule Dossier do
  defstruct account: "", summary: "", findings: [], sources: [], verified?: false
end

The brain gets two tools and lives in a sandbox so `:net` is the only cap it holds:

@research grant: [:net], memory: "256mb", timeout: 120_000

sandbox :research, @research do
  agent :researcher do
    model "minimax/minimax-m3"

    system """
    Research B2B accounts in a strict loop: PLAN the questions worth chasing,
    SEARCH and read the best result, VERIFY every claim against its source (drop
    what you can't cite), then SYNTHESIZE a cited summary. Never invent a fact.
    """

    tool :search, do: (query -> Search.web(query, limit: 6))
    tool :read,   do: (url -> Fetch.readable(url))
  end
end

The loop is an explicit flow so each stage is inspectable and testable:

flow :research_account do
  step :plan,       from: :lead,   do: Researcher.plan(lead)
  step :search,     from: :plan,   do: parallel(questions, &Researcher.investigate/1)
  step :verify,     from: :search, do: Enum.filter(candidates, &Researcher.supported?/1)
  step :synthesize, from: :verify, do: {:ok, %Dossier{summary: Researcher.write_summary(verified), verified?: true}}
end

`verify` is non-negotiable: it re-opens each source and confirms the claim. Because
every finding is a `{:fact, claim, url}` tuple and `verified?` only flips after the
filter, a test can assert no finished dossier holds an uncited fact. Next:
[[Reflexion]].
